# Architecture law

If unsure where code goes: add a CashFlowKit use case + port, implement the port in CashFlowData, and call it from a Feature ViewModel. Never put money math or networking in a SwiftUI View.

## Modules

- `Packages/CashFlowKit` — pure domain (Foundation only)
- `Packages/CashFlowData` — SwiftData, URLSession, Keychain, Demo, SimpleFIN, Sync
- `ExpenseTracking` — SwiftUI features + `DependencyContainer` (only concrete wiring site)

## SOLID applies to every file

Do not add multi-purpose types, bypass ports with concretes in Features, or widen protocols “for convenience.”

## Money

Use `Decimal` only. Never `Double`/`Float` for amounts in domain, data, or UI models (chart plotting may convert at the view edge only).

## Errors

Throw `CashFlowError` from CashFlowData. Every case carries a user-facing `errorDescription`. Features display failures only via `CashFlowError.userFacingMessage(for:fallback:)` — no parallel mappers, no raw `"CashFlowError error N"` banners. Foundation Models mapping stays in CashFlowData and finishes as `.intelligence(message:)` / `.intelligenceUnavailable`.

## Transactions list

Keyset pagination (page size 50). Predicate-scoped filters (account, date, category). Preformatted `TransactionRowModel` strings. No full-table fetch.

## Verification before done

Run package tests and `scripts/check_architecture.sh`. Prefer XcodeBuildMCP `test_sim` / `build_sim` when touching the app target.
